==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|claritee}}, borrowed from {{bor|en|fro|clarté}}, from {{der|en|la|clāritās}}, from {{m|la|clārus|t=clear}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈklæɹɪti/}}
* {{rhymes|en|æɹɪti}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The state or measure of being [[clear]], either in [[appearance]], [[thought]] or [[style]]; [[lucidity]].
#: {{ux|en|She dreamed, with great '''clarity''', that she had been seen her own death.}}
#: {{ux|en|Lack of '''clarity''' on the part of the teacher will cause confusion among the students.}}
#: {{syn|en|clearness|obviousness|transparency}}
#: {{ant|en|confusion}}

